{"agent":"fix-select","data":{"by":"fix-select","evidence":{"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"note":"Claim: ordering the ready set by (interrupted/orphaned first, then bug, then phase-less task, then priority) makes `ddflow next` offer a mix of those tiers in that order (B4e2a112a97). Mechanism: the schedule already sorts the ready set by registered ordering keys (core/schedule order_key); adding recover_first and unphased_first keys ahead of bugs_first/priority makes the offer order the fill order. Falsifier: a generic task at a lower priority than an interrupted/bug/unphased peer offered before it would refute. Probe: seeded {STALLED (interrupted), FIXBUG (bugfix), LOOSE (no phase), FEAT (priority 5)} and plan().ready == [STALLED, FIXBUG, LOOSE, FEAT]; fill_order() == same. CONFIRMED.","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/core/schedule/_filters.py":"100644 a0a838057b9453db5f6fb399b25d733372973db5","ddflow/services/orchestrator.py":"100644 5e636e1a3cd8b0ec4670977ee2cf306251997227","tests/test_orchestrator_fill_order.py":"100644 a23cdd7ac2a9c98c51125bfc535c3e5c3ea1b88b"},"tree_sha":"84da233f4200+clean"},"gate":"research","reason":""},"id":"e15ddcdf2206a2941427928a8","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":136357,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B4e2a112a97","ts":"2026-11-04T19:30:06.524950Z"}
